  "name": "Question 3",
  "problem": "Given that $A=QR$ is a QR factorization of a $5\\times 4$ matrix $A$ with linearly independent columns, which of the following statements are true?\n\n- The columns of $Q$ are orthogonal\n- $Q$ is a $5\\times 5$ matrix\n- $R$ is a  square  matrix",
  "worked_solution": "Recall that if $A=QR$ is a  QR factorization of an $m\\times n$ matrix $A,$ then\n\n$$\n{A}_{m\\times n}={Q}_{m\\times n}\\times {R}_{n\\times n},\n$$\n\nwhere \n\n- $Q$ is an $m\\times n$ matrix whose columns form an orthonormal basis of $\\text{Col}(A)$\n\n- $R$ is an $n\\times n$ upper triangular matrix\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements.\n\n- Statement I is true. Indeed, since the columns of $Q$ form an orthonormal basis, they are orthogonal.\n\n- Statement II is false. $Q$ should be a $5\\times 4$  matrix.\n\n- Statement III is true. Indeed, $R$ must be a $4\\times 4$ upper triangular matrix.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\"",
